@coderabbitai <!-- aidevops:review-thread-response:PRRT_kwDOQSEXLM6w-XEg -->
Addressed in `.agents/scripts/protected-label-guard.sh:178-194`: publication now uses a nonblocking kernel `flock` via Python's `fcntl` on an inherited descriptor. The stable lock inode is never unlinked; descriptor closure releases ownership after a crash without age-based reclamation. A separate filename avoids legacy orphaned directory locks, and acquisition failures emit a busy/unavailable diagnostic. Invalid configuration behavior remains unchanged.

Verified with `bash .agents/scripts/tests/test-protected-label-guard.sh`, including legacy orphan recovery, live-lock exclusion, concurrent publication, and SIGKILL recovery. ShellCheck passed for all four changed scripts.

@coderabbitai <!-- aidevops:review-thread-response:PRRT_kwDOQSEXLM6w-XEk -->
Addressed in `.agents/scripts/pulse-nmr-approval.sh:2145-2148`: failed flap preflight now logs an explicit auto-approval deferral before returning. The successful path and empty result on deferral are unchanged; no approval lock or marker is posted.

Verified with `bash .agents/scripts/tests/test-pulse-nmr-maintainer-authority.sh` (36 checks, zero failures), including the new deferral-log assertion alongside existing no-lock/no-marker checks. ShellCheck passed.

@coderabbitai Fixed in commit 96cc0151c. Confirmed the filename-only invocation failed before assertions; `.agents/scripts/tests/test-pulse-dispatch-worker-launch-bundle.sh:8` now uses `dirname` to handle that case.

Verified: `bash test-pulse-dispatch-worker-launch-bundle.sh` from the tests directory and `bash .agents/scripts/tests/test-pulse-dispatch-worker-launch-bundle.sh` from the repository root both pass. `bash -n`, `git diff --check`, and commit/push hooks (including typecheck) passed. Standalone ShellCheck was unavailable because its wrapper could not find the real binary.

